    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [-360, -390],
      "size": [700, 340],
      "title": "How this workflow selects model and references",
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Persistent native references + memory chain\n\n**Model selection is automatic:** an empty Reference Bank loads FL2VA; any image, video, or audio reference selects Ref2VA. `start_image` is deliberately separate: it is the physical chain keyframe, not a numbered reference.\n\n**Reference labels:** native order is images (`<Picture N>`), then each reference video's paired audio immediately before that video (`<Audio N>`, `<Video N>`), then standalone audio (`<Audio N>`). Use the generated order consistently in every shot prompt.\n\n**Practical RTX 5090 profile:** use 1-3 images plus one clean 6-12 second voice reference; `ref_image_size=match`; 960x544 / 243 frames. The native 9 images + 3 videos + 3 standalone audios are supported, but persistent video context increases VRAM and attention cost on every step. Start with one short video reference only after the image/voice path is stable.\n\nThe sampler still chains with the previous final frame and preserves a first-shot visual anchor plus recent memory frames."
      ],
      "color": "#24364b",
      "bgcolor": "#13202f"
    },
